ue row\n    issue_row = page.get_by_role('row').filter(has=page.get_by_role('link', name='accessibility statement', exact=False))\n    # Click on the issue link to open it\n    issue_link = issue_row.get_by_role('link').first\n    await issue_link.click()\n    await page.wait_for_load_state('networkidle')\n    \n    # Step 4: Assign the issue to Rohan\n    # Look for an assignee button or dropdown\n    assignee_button = page.get_by_role('button', name='Assign')\n    await assignee_button.click()\n    # Wait for dropdown to appear\n    await page.wait_for_timeout(1000)\n    # Search for Rohan in the assignee dropdown\n    search_box = page.get_by_role('textbox', name='Search users')\n    await search_box.fill('Rohan')\n    await page.wait_for_timeout(500)\n    # Select Rohan from the results\n    rohan_option = page.get_by_role('option', name='Rohan')\n    await rohan_option.click()\n    # Save the assignment\n    save_button = page.get_by_role('button', name='Save')\n    await save_button.click()\n    await page.wait_for_load_state('networkidle')\n</code>\n\n<exception>\n'TimeoutError': Locator.click: Timeout 5000ms exceeded.\nCall log:\n  - waiting for get_by_role(\"button\", name=\"Assign\")\n\n</exception>\n\n---\n\n<reasoning>\nI am currently on the issue page for '[Feature suggestion] Support linking to an accessibility statement (#4)' in the a11y-webring.club project. The task is to assign this issue to Rohan. From the accessibility tree, I can see that the issue sidebar contains a link 'Rohan Kumar' under the complementary 'issue' section, which suggests Rohan might already be assigned or mentioned. However, the task requires assigning the issue to Rohan, so I need to check the current assignee and assign it if not already done. Looking at the tree, there is a button 'Issue actions' with expanded: False, which likely contains an 'Assign' option. I should click this button to open the dropdown, then select 'Assign' and choose Rohan. Alternatively, there might 